      "description": "University Assistant (PhD position) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (PhD position) Start date/duration: as soon as possible for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Statistics Extent of employment: 20 hours per week; will be increased to 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed Job Description: Your responsibilities: PhD thesis in the field of statistics Independent research in the field of probabilistic modelling, statistical inference and machine learning, with potential applications to practical problems Independent teaching Supporting research work, participation in research projects, and assistance with teaching and examination duties Training and professional development Administrative duties Your profile: A relevant completed Master, Magister or Diplom degree in the fields of statistics, data science, mathematics or economics, with a specialisation in statistics or econometrics Very good knowledge of mathematics, particularly probability theory and statistics Proven programming experience in a high-level programming language (particularly R or Python) Excellent command of English, excellent command of German is a plus Teamwork and communication skills Please include with your application a comprising a covering letter, CV and academic transcripts and a written outline of your proposed dissertation topic (approx. 1 page) Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/VWL-15978 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#dissertationsstellen Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agr