    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=15981": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Doctorate/PhD)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer (Doctorate/PhD) Back PDF output Apply online Senior Lecturer (Doctorate/PhD) Start date/duration: from 01.10.2026 for 4 years, possibility for a permanent position depending on requirement and performance evaluation Administrative unit: Department of Mathematics Extent of employment: 40 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Independently delivering courses and conducting examinations with focus on probability and algebra (16 semester hours) Assisting with organisational and administrative tasks as well as evaluation procedures Supervising students, including supervising Bachelor theses Further training Your profile: Completed a relevant doctoral or PhD programme Good communication and teamwork skills Positive communication with staff and students Ability to motivate students Organisational skills Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/MIP-15981 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#senior-lecturer-doktorat-phd Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 5.014 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 14.10.2026 stating the code MIP-15981 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Christian Bargetz Email: christian.bargetz@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
    },
    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=15897": {
      "title": "Senior Scientist (Doctorate/PhD)",
      "description": "Senior Scientist (Doctorate/PhD) Back PDF output Apply online Senior Scientist (Doctorate/PhD) Start date/duration: from 02.12.2026 for xx years, possibility for a permanent position in case of probation and continued need Administrative unit: Department of Systematic Theology Extent of employment: 40 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Independent research in the field of systematic theology, particularly dogmatics, with a focus on theological and philosophical anthropology Delivering high-quality, research-led teaching independently in German and English in Digital Society (DigiSoc) and Dogmatics Conducting examinations Contributing to organisational and administrative tasks especially in Digital Society (DigiSoc) Supervision of students Your profile: PhD in Theology, specialising in Dogmatics Language skills: English and German International network in research collaborations (particularly in the areas mentioned above) Teaching experience; Skills in working with students; ability to work as part of a team desirable qualification: PhD in Philosophy Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/THEOL-15897 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#senior-scientists-doktorat-phd Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 5.014 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 15.10.2026 stating the code THEOL-15897 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Assoz.-Prof. Mag. Dr. Nikolaus Wandinger Phone: +43-(0)512 507-85267 Email: nikolaus.wandinger@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
    },
