    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=15963": {
      "title": "University Assistant (postdoc)",
      "description": "University Assistant (postdoc) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (postdoc) Start date/duration: as soon as possible for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Atmospheric and Cryospheric Sciences Extent of employment: 40 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Independent scientific research in the field of dynamic meteorology, focusing on the influence of diabatic processes on synoptic scales and their interactions on mesoscale and planetary scales. Publications in internationally recognised journals Independent delivery of teaching modules and conducting examinations Supervision of students Participation in academic self-governance Contributing to the development and maintenance of the research group's software library Further training Your profile: PhD in a discipline of atmospheric sciences (such as meteorology, atmospheric physics, climatology) or a related discipline Sound knowledge of dynamic meteorology, particularly at synoptic scales Knowledge of extratropical storms, jet streams and storm tracks would be an advantage Knowledge of the interaction between weather and climate variability would be an advantage Knowledge of diabatic processes, particularly moist-diabatic ones, and their influence on synoptic, meso- and planetary scales would be an advantage Ability to combine theory with data analysis from numerical simulations, reanalyses or climate models would be an advantage Broad programming skills in at least one high-level programming language knowledge of Fortran and Python is an advantage Knowledge of high-performance computing is an advantage Knowledge of AI methods is an advantage Experience in planning, implementing and leading scientific projects is an advantage Good written and spoken communication skills in English, proficiency in German is an advantage Experience in university teaching is an advantage Competence in supervising students is an advantage Teaching skills would be an advantage Communication and teamwork skills Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/GEO-15963 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#post-doc Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 5.014 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 21.10.2026 stating the code GEO-15963 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Thomas Spengler Email: thomas.spengler@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
    },
    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=16000": {
      "title": "University Assistant (postdoc)",
      "description": "University Assistant (postdoc) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (postdoc) Start date/duration: from 01.12.2026 for 6 years Administrative unit: Department of Archaeology Extent of employment: 40 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Independent research in historical archaeology, with a focus on social archaeology and digital methods of interdisciplinary source analysis Collaboration on projects run by the Chair of Historical Archaeology (helping to develop new methodological and theoretical approaches; devising project concepts in line with the research priorities of the Historical Archaeology research group) Independent publication and lecturing activities Securing external funding Contributing to the organisation of conferences and knowledge transfer events, as well as academic self-governance Independent teaching and conducting examinations within the BA and MA \"Archaeologies\" curriculum in the field of Historical Archaeology (Middle Ages to the present day); (co-)supervision of student theses Your profile: Completed doctoral or PhD studies in an archaeological discipline with a dissertation focusing on Historical Archaeology or Contemporary Archaeology Demonstrated research activities in the historical archaeology of the recent past in Central Europe Experience in organising and carrying out field research projects as well as transfer-oriented projects Experience in developing methodologies for historical archaeology and digital archaeology (data management, geographic information systems) is desirable Potential links to the research priorities of the Chair of Historical Archaeology are desirable Experience in securing external funding is desirable Initial experience in university teaching and supervising student theses is desirable Strong ability to work in a team, excellent communication skills and organisational talent Please submit the following application documents: Cover letter (max. 2 pages), CV including a list of publications, Outline of a proposed project in historical archaeology (max. 2 pages), PhD thesis, Degree certificates Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/PHIL-HIST-16000 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#post-doc Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 5.014 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 23.10.2026 stating the code PHIL-HIST-16000 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Univ.-Prof. Mag. Dr. Barbara Hausmair Phone: +4351250740818 Email: barbara.hausmair@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
